@* Shown on every page of a demo session, so a walkthrough can never be
   mistaken for a real account: the data here goes away at sign-out. The
   way out is the same sign-out form as everywhere else, which erases the
   demo account and lands on the sign-in page. *@

<AuthorizeView>
    @if (CurrentUser.IsDemo(context.User))
    {
        <div class="demo-banner" role="note">
            <span class="demo-banner-icon"><AppIcon Name="info" Size="inherit" /></span>
            <p class="demo-banner-text">
                <strong>Demo account.</strong> Everything you add here is erased when the demo ends.
                Sign in with Google to keep your spots.
            </p>
            <SignOutForm ButtonClass="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm demo-banner-action" Label="End demo" />
        </div>
    }
</AuthorizeView>
